14. unique_ptr
English

unique_ptr provides exclusive ownership of a dynamically allocated object. When the unique_ptr is destroyed, the managed object is automatically deleted.

Hindi

unique_ptr किसी dynamically allocated object की exclusive ownership रखता है। unique_ptr destroy होने पर managed object automatically delete हो जाता है।

Example
#include <iostream>
#include <memory>
using namespace std;


int main()
{
    unique_ptr<int> p = make_unique<int>(100);


    cout << *p << endl;


    return 0;
}

जब main() समाप्त होगा, p destroy होगा और managed memory automatically release हो जाएगी।

Output
100

Note -->
unique_ptr normally copy not possible because ownership 2 same objct not possible.
but ownership move possible.

std::unique_ptr<int> p2 = std::move(p);


15. shared_ptr
English

shared_ptr allows multiple smart pointers to share ownership of the same dynamically allocated object. The object is destroyed when the last owning shared_ptr is destroyed or reset.

Hindi

shared_ptr में multiple smart pointers एक ही object की shared ownership रख सकते हैं। जब last owning shared_ptr भी destroy/reset हो जाता है, तब object की memory release हो जाती है।

Example :
#include <memory>

int main() {
    std::shared_ptr<int> p1 = std::make_shared<int>(10);

    std::shared_ptr<int> p2 = p1;

    return 0;
}

Example
#include <iostream>
#include <memory>
using namespace std;


int main()
{
    shared_ptr<int> p1 = make_shared<int>(100);
    shared_ptr<int> p2 = p1;


    cout << *p1 << endl;
    cout << *p2 << endl;


    cout << "Owners: " << p1.use_count() << endl;


    return 0;
}

Output
100
100
Owners: 2

16. weak_ptr
English

weak_ptr is a non-owning smart pointer used to observe an object managed by shared_ptr without increasing its reference count.

Hindi

weak_ptr किसी shared_ptr द्वारा managed object को observe करता है, लेकिन उसकी ownership नहीं लेता और reference count को increase नहीं करता।

#include <memory>

int main() {
    std::shared_ptr<int> p1 = std::make_shared<int>(10);

    std::weak_ptr<int> p2 = p1;

    return 0;
}

Main Purpose

यह विशेष रूप से circular references को avoid करने में useful है।

unique_ptr-->

unique_ptr is a smart pointer that provides exclusive ownership of an object.
unique_ptr ऐसा smart pointer है जो किसी object की exclusive यानी केवल एक owner वाली ownership प्रदान करता है।

shared_ptr-->

shared_ptr is a smart pointer that allows multiple pointers to share ownership of an object.
shared_ptr ऐसा smart pointer है जो कई pointers को एक object की ownership share करने देता है।

weak_ptr-->

weak_ptr is a smart pointer that observes an object managed by shared_ptr without owning it.
weak_ptr ऐसा smart pointer है जो shared_ptr के object को observe करता है लेकिन उसकी ownership नहीं लेता।

RAII → Object lifetime से resource management
unique_ptr → One owner
shared_ptr → Multiple owners
weak_ptr → Observer, no ownership

17. Garbage Collection vs C++ RAII

| Garbage Collection                                           | C++ RAII                                                              |
| ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Automatically reclaims unreachable memory                    | Resource is tied to object lifetime                                   |
| Runtime GC system identifies garbage                         | Destructor automatically performs cleanup                             |
| Common in Java/C#                                            | Fundamental C++ technique                                             |
| Exact cleanup time may depend on GC                          | Cleanup is normally deterministic at object lifetime end              |
| Programmer usually doesn't manually call GC-managed `delete` | C++ uses destructors/smart pointers for automatic resource management |


18. Garbage collection vs Destructor -->
| Garbage Collection                                          | Destructor                                               |
| ----------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| Memory-management mechanism                                 | Special member function                                  |
| Finds/reclaims garbage or unreachable objects in GC systems | Performs cleanup for a particular object                 |
| Usually automatic                                           | Called automatically when object lifetime ends           |
| Not part of standard C++ memory management                  | Built into C++ object lifetime mechanism                 |
| Can manage many unreachable objects                         | Handles cleanup associated with one object's destruction |

19. Advantages of Garbage Collection
1. Automatic Memory Management

English: Reduces the need for explicit memory deallocation.
Hindi: Programmer को manually memory release करने की जरूरत कम होती है।

2. Reduces Certain Memory Leaks

English: Unreachable objects can be automatically reclaimed.
Hindi: Unreachable objects की memory automatically reclaim हो सकती है।

3. Easier Programming

English: Developers can focus more on application logic rather than manual memory management.
Hindi: Programmer का focus memory management के बजाय application logic पर ज्यादा रह सकता है।

4. Safer Memory Management

English: It can prevent some errors related to forgotten deallocation.
Hindi: Memory release भूलने से होने वाली कुछ problems को कम कर सकता है।

20. Disadvantages of Garbage Collection
1. Runtime Overhead

GC को memory scan और reclaim करने के लिए processing करनी पड़ती है।

2. Less Predictable Cleanup Timing

GC-managed objects का exact cleanup time programmer के direct control में नहीं होता।

3. Additional Memory Usage

GC को tracking और management के लिए additional resources की आवश्यकता हो सकती है।

4. Not Available as Standard Automatic GC in C++

Standard C++ में Java जैसी built-in automatic garbage collection system नहीं है।

