24. Most Important BCA Exam Questions
Q1. What is Garbage Collection?

Garbage Collection is an automatic memory-management technique that identifies unused or unreachable memory and reclaims it.

Q2. Does C++ support Garbage Collection?

Standard C++ does not provide a built-in automatic garbage collector like Java or C#. C++ primarily uses RAII, destructors, and explicit/deterministic resource management.

Q3. What is Garbage?

Garbage is memory or an object that is no longer useful/reachable but still occupies memory.

Q4. What is Memory Leak?

A memory leak occurs when allocated memory is no longer needed but is not released.

Q5. What is the role of delete?

delete destroys a single object allocated with new and releases its storage.

Q6. What is RAII?

RAII is a C++ resource-management technique that ties resource lifetime to object lifetime and automatically releases the resource when the object is destroyed.

Q7. Is Destructor a Garbage Collector?

No. A destructor performs cleanup for an object's lifetime; it is not an automatic garbage-collection system.

